+/* There is deliberately no -_print here. This class used to override it with
+   a copy of GSEPSPrintOperation's, which draws the whole rect as a single
+   sheet:
+
+     [_view beginPageInRect: _rect atPlacement: NSMakePoint(0,0)];
+     [_view displayRectIgnoringOpacity: _rect inContext: [self context]];
+     // FIXME: Output comes out up-side-down
+
+   That is right for EPS, which is single-sheet by definition, and wrong for
+   PDF, which is not. It never asked the view for -knowsPageRange: or
+   -rectForPage:, so a view that paginates itself came out as one sheet; and
+   because it applied no transform, it also never reached the flip that
+   -_displayPageInRect:withInfo:knowsPageRange: applies for a flipped view --
+   the cause of the upside-down output its own comment recorded. Locking focus
+   still calls GSWSetViewIsFlipped(ctxt, YES), so the backend compensated for a
+   flip that was not in the CTM, mirroring the glyphs as well as the layout.
+
+   NSPrintOperation's own -_print does all of this correctly and needs nothing
+   from this subclass: -_runOperation has already made -createContext's context
+   current, and -_printPaginateWithInfo:knowsRange: sets NSPrintSheetBounds
+   itself. Inheriting it fixes both the orientation and the pagination. */
 
